```bash
podkit cluster login .                       # kubeconfig for {{ cloud.clusterName }}
podkit doctor .                              # tools, cloud CLI and cluster access
podkit pod deploy .                          # kubectl path
podkit pod deploy . -m terraform             # or the Terraform path (creates the cloud identity too)
podkit pod status . ; podkit pod logs . -f
podkit destroy . --everything                # workload + secrets + TLS + identity + namespace
```
{% if identity.enabled %}

Cloud identity: `podkit identity apply .` creates it with Terraform and stores `IDENTITY_ID` in `pod.env`;
`podkit pod deploy .` then binds it to the ServiceAccount.
{% endif %}
{% if tls %}

TLS: `podkit tls status {{ namespace }}` shows the CA, truststore and keystores; `podkit tls rotate .` reissues this pod's certificate.
{% endif %}
